# {{projectName}}

Standalone Playwright test project generated by
[qa-ai](https://github.com/) from a crawled SiteModel and an AI-authored
TestPlan. It is self-contained — it has its own `package.json` and can be
committed and run on its own.

**Target:** {{baseUrl}}

## Run

```bash
npm install
npx playwright install chromium   # first run only
npm test                          # headless
npm run test:headed               # watch the browser
npm run report                    # open the last HTML report
```

## Layout

- `src/fixtures/base.ts` — the test fixture. Import `test` / `expect` from here,
  never from `@playwright/test` directly. Provides a `consoleErrors` fixture.
- `src/pages/` — Page Object classes (one per page), extending `BasePage`.
- `tests/` — spec files, mirroring the app URL structure. `tests/data/` holds
  JSON test data. `tests/seed.spec.ts` is the environment baseline.
- `playwright.config.ts` — chromium desktop, HTML + JSON reporters. The JSON
  `results.json` is the machine handoff `qa-ai heal` consumes.
- `generation-manifest.json` — maps spec files back to their source TestCase
  ids (used by `qa-ai run-generated` / `qa-ai heal`).

## Credentials

Credentials are read from environment variables (never committed). Copy
`.env.example` to `.env` and fill in the values, or export them in your shell
before running.

## Conventions

Locators follow a strict priority (`getByRole` → `getByLabel` →
`getByPlaceholder` → `getByTestId` → `getByText`); CSS/XPath are avoided. Each
test carries a `// qa-ai:test_id=… signature=…` traceability comment linking it
to the source plan.
